WEBVTT

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:12.330
You have to stay inside, Mii-kun.

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:14.350
What is <i>that</i>?

00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:19.750
Why is there a lizard on Tazuki's desk?

00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:23.290
This isn't real.

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:25.550
Did I scare you?

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:27.490
It's a really lifelike toy.

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:29.080
Was this your doing, Suzuki?

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:30.550
It's really well-made.

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:33.050
That's what the maker's known for.

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:36.740
Urokozawa Gengorou-sensei 
is the best there is

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:39.290
when it comes to realistic reptiles.

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:43.150
All this quality for just a capsule toy!

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:43.810
<i>I wonder if he's curious about it.</i>

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:46.040
Come on, man, listen to me!

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:46.800
Nope.

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:48.780
Come on, please.

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:51.260
Here, I'll let you have this one, Kashiwagi.

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:53.660
Th-Thanks.

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:54.450
Don't need it.

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:57.110
Come on, just keep it.

00:00:56.570 --> 00:01:01.200
<b>Children's Park</b>

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:38.300
#5
Go Away Kindness, Go Away Fear

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:38.250
I don't know what to do with this thing.

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:40.020
Why don't you show it off in your room?

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:42.960
Mii seems awfully happy.

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:43.860
Yeah.

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:46.720
I didn't think he'd be interested in lizards.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:50.720
Although I don't know if you 
can call it a lizard anymore.

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:52.860
He's good at wrapping things.

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:53.230
Mummy

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:57.990
I did it

00:02:56.650 --> 00:02:57.990
I did it

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:02.180
Mii-kun, the tissue is 
coming off at the tail.

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:13.420
It's okay.

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:15.640
You'll get better at wrapping with practice.

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:18.190
Hey, you did the body perfectly.

00:03:18.190 --> 00:03:20.740
Why don't we try wrapping the tail together?

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:23.090
<i>What are you, a parent?</i>

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:24.720
Huh?

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:26.590
You gave him a lizard?

00:03:26.590 --> 00:03:28.020
Want one, Tanaka?

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:29.540
Nah...

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:30.980
Sorry.

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:37.660
Yume-chan, there's a bug on your back!

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:38.710
Really? Get it!

00:03:38.710 --> 00:03:40.190
Get it!

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:41.730
No way!

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:43.240
Please, get it!

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:44.950
There, I got it.

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:47.370
You're safe now.

00:03:47.850 --> 00:03:49.620
Thank you!

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:51.930
Thank you so much!

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:55.300
You're overreacting over a bug.

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:06.280
L-L-Lizard, no!

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:11.560
Even though she's okay with bugs?

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:19.820
Stay inside!

00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:24.580
I don't know if it's a good idea 
to keep bringing Mii to school.

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:27.410
But Mii-kun gets lonely.

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:29.080
It's been two months.

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:30.710
He must have gotten used to Japan by now.

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:34.670
I think you should give him 
practice staying at home alone.

00:04:35.090 --> 00:04:38.380
Yeah, I wouldn't have to 
bring him to school every day

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:40.660
if he could stay at home by himself.

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:41.420
Right?

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:46.060
I wouldn't have to worry about people 
finding out about him, either.

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:49.430
Considering the fact that we're going 
to be living together going forward...

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:53.810
Even if I get in a battle with the stuff 
my dad mails me, and I get injured,

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:55.580
I can feel safe staying at the hospital

00:04:55.580 --> 00:04:58.720
Don't you ever consider escaping?

00:04:59.990 --> 00:05:02.870
I think we'll practice 
having him stay home alone.

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:04.940
I think that's for the better.

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:08.410
If only there were a preschool 
for these kinds of creatures.

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:10.200
I figured you'd say that.

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:13.080
Oh, yeah, aren't you going 
to bring Conny to school?

00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:17.710
That kid's too rambunctious.

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:20.090
He'd end both of our lives.

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:24.470
Hey.

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:27.630
I was so scared.

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:29.900
You hate lizards that badly, huh?

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:31.580
But it was just a toy.

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:32.720
I hate them.

00:05:33.030 --> 00:05:35.580
Lizards are lizards, toy or not.

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:38.500
What's wrong?

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:39.610
Another lizard?

00:05:40.550 --> 00:05:42.610
It's a crêpe shop!

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:44.610
I'm home.

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:48.430
Kaede-san, what do you want for dinner today?

00:05:48.430 --> 00:05:49.620
Huh?

00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:53.620
Pochi's gone, too.

00:05:56.270 --> 00:05:57.620
Kaede-san?

00:06:01.010 --> 00:06:02.920
I wonder if she went for a walk or something.

00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:15.660
I can't eat any more...

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:16.620
<i>Sleep talking?!</i>

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:18.270
<i>Napping in a casket?!</i>

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:21.840
<i>Oh, yeah, she pulled an 
all-nighter last night.</i>

00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:23.670
<i>I should give her some space.</i>

00:06:28.940 --> 00:06:31.670
Okay, I'm going to go shopping for dinner.

00:06:33.670 --> 00:06:38.670
I'll be home by the time the short hand 
is here and the long hand is here.

00:06:41.670 --> 00:06:43.540
Can you stay home without crying?

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:49.050
If you can stay home without crying,

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:52.300
I'll read you <i>two</i> bedtime stories tonight.

00:06:58.580 --> 00:07:00.720
<i>He's so happy.</i>

00:07:04.310 --> 00:07:05.650
Okay, see you.

00:07:14.260 --> 00:07:16.060
I'll get home quick.

00:07:18.850 --> 00:07:20.290
I'm home.

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:21.880
Mom, get this...

00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:24.420
There was a crêpe shop on my way home.

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:26.600
You like crêpes, so...

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:36.060
A cockroach showed up in the kitchen. 
I'm going to buy insecticide.
It was so huge and scary!

00:07:32.570 --> 00:07:37.060
"A cockroach showed up in the kitchen. 
I'm going to buy insecticide."

00:07:37.630 --> 00:07:41.510
Oh, I could have taken the cockroach outside.

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:46.210
I guess I'll have the crêpes 
after Mom gets home.

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:20.870
<i>It's a gigantic lizard!</i>

00:08:19.220 --> 00:08:19.720
<b>Li</b>

00:08:19.720 --> 00:08:20.220
<b>Liza</b>

00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:21.980
<b>Lizard!</b>

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:23.980
Help!

00:08:55.220 --> 00:08:57.550
Ow...

00:09:01.810 --> 00:09:03.850
I ran too fast.

00:09:06.430 --> 00:09:09.320
W-Wait, wait, wait!

00:09:09.590 --> 00:09:11.940
I can't stand lizards!

00:09:14.810 --> 00:09:17.530
Mom, there's a huge lizard in my room.

00:09:18.010 --> 00:09:21.340
She's out right now!

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:30.420
Stay back! Stay back! Stay Back! Stay Back!

00:09:30.420 --> 00:09:32.420
Stay back!

00:09:39.630 --> 00:09:41.430
I wonder if I hurt it.

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:43.430
Huh?

00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:45.930
It's gone.

00:10:05.860 --> 00:10:08.770
All right, I can make
it home in plenty of time.

00:10:08.770 --> 00:10:10.500
I hope Mii-kun's okay.

00:10:14.590 --> 00:10:16.580
That was loud.

00:10:16.580 --> 00:10:18.470
I wonder what's going on in that house.

00:10:18.470 --> 00:10:21.850
Stop it!

00:10:23.490 --> 00:10:24.900
Sorry.

00:10:25.380 --> 00:10:26.220
Sora-chan!

00:10:26.220 --> 00:10:27.350
Motegi-san?

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:30.350
Calm down.

00:10:30.760 --> 00:10:32.720
There, take a deep breath.

00:10:32.720 --> 00:10:35.110
A-A deep breath?

00:10:38.800 --> 00:10:40.740
Wait, that's the wrong breathing technique.

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:41.620
No!

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:44.490
L-Lizard! Lizard!

00:10:44.880 --> 00:10:45.750
Huh?

00:10:45.750 --> 00:10:46.620
A lizard?

00:10:46.820 --> 00:10:48.190
There's a lizard?

00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:51.250
You hate lizards, huh?

00:10:52.740 --> 00:10:54.130
Should I catch it?

00:10:55.580 --> 00:10:57.120
Your head's going to fall off.

00:10:57.120 --> 00:10:58.630
Seriously, calm down.

00:10:59.080 --> 00:11:00.700
Is it okay if I go in?

00:11:00.700 --> 00:11:02.750
You're more than welcome to!

00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:05.890
Thank you for...

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:10.920
What happened, Motegi-san?

00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:14.400
I-I-I was trying to get 
the l-lizard to go away.

00:11:14.800 --> 00:11:17.330
And that's how this happened?

00:11:19.060 --> 00:11:20.710
<i>She's scary...</i>

00:11:20.710 --> 00:11:23.120
<i>I feel bad for said lizard.</i>

00:11:24.390 --> 00:11:28.660
<i>I have a feeling it's already 
been squashed under the shoe box.</i>

00:11:29.010 --> 00:11:30.660
<i>I don't want to see it...</i>

00:11:31.100 --> 00:11:33.800
Motegi-san, are you strong?

00:11:33.800 --> 00:11:35.270
Y-Yeah.

00:11:35.850 --> 00:11:40.350
If the lizard popped out, or if it turns 
out to have been squashed to a pulp,

00:11:40.350 --> 00:11:45.210
please don't throw a shoe box at 
me or throw me at the lizard.

00:11:48.230 --> 00:11:49.250
Okay...

00:11:49.250 --> 00:11:51.030
<i>Her hesitation frightens me.</i>

00:12:02.380 --> 00:12:03.900
D-Did you find it?

00:12:03.900 --> 00:12:05.930
No, I can't find it.

00:12:08.070 --> 00:12:09.630
Is this a huge orange?

00:12:17.340 --> 00:12:18.930
No way, it's a dragon!

00:12:19.740 --> 00:12:22.650
Hey, Motegi-san, when you say 
"lizard," do you mean this guy?

00:12:22.650 --> 00:12:24.570
That guy!

00:12:24.890 --> 00:12:26.920
A-Are you okay, Motegi-san?

00:12:26.920 --> 00:12:28.410
This isn't a lizard.

00:12:28.410 --> 00:12:31.270
Wait, I'm not ready emotionally!

00:12:33.680 --> 00:12:34.520
Motegi-san!

00:12:35.150 --> 00:12:39.390
<i>Shoot, I never realized she 
hated lizards to this extent.</i>

00:12:41.040 --> 00:12:43.530
Huh? What? Upstairs?

00:12:44.810 --> 00:12:46.020
No?

00:12:47.970 --> 00:12:48.890
Stairs?

00:12:50.180 --> 00:12:51.540
Tumbled?

00:12:52.460 --> 00:12:53.360
Knee?

00:12:54.240 --> 00:12:55.070
Hurt?

00:12:58.290 --> 00:12:59.590
Hey, Motegi-san...

00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:03.310
Did you fall down the stairs 
and hurt your knee?

00:13:04.790 --> 00:13:07.260
He seems pretty worried.

00:13:07.870 --> 00:13:09.100
Worried?

00:13:12.430 --> 00:13:14.600
Come to think of it,

00:13:15.750 --> 00:13:17.720
even when I was crying in my room...

00:13:21.170 --> 00:13:26.870
Did you come after me 
because you were worried?

00:13:28.600 --> 00:13:30.660
I-I'm sorry.

00:13:30.660 --> 00:13:35.370
I ran away and did terrible things to you.

00:13:36.070 --> 00:13:40.560
I should have heard you out, 
even if you're a lizard.

00:13:40.560 --> 00:13:41.820
He's not a lizard, though.

00:13:41.820 --> 00:13:43.470
I'm sorry.

00:13:43.470 --> 00:13:46.380
I can't believe what I've done.

00:13:52.380 --> 00:13:55.530
I think he's trying to tell 
you not to worry about it.

00:13:57.530 --> 00:14:01.900
It looks like he's really worried 
because you're so bummed out.

00:14:13.870 --> 00:14:14.830
I'm sorry.

00:14:14.940 --> 00:14:16.150
I'm sorry.

00:14:16.620 --> 00:14:19.140
I'm really, really sorry.

00:14:19.450 --> 00:14:20.480
But...

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:24.150
Thanks for worrying for me so much.

00:14:24.530 --> 00:14:26.740
You've made me feel better.

00:14:29.130 --> 00:14:30.290
Thanks.

00:14:55.610 --> 00:14:56.700
Are you okay?

00:14:56.700 --> 00:14:57.770
Can you breathe okay?

00:15:00.440 --> 00:15:02.480
Do you have one at your 
place, too, Sora-chan?

00:15:02.480 --> 00:15:05.190
Yeah, although it's not a dragon.

00:15:05.190 --> 00:15:06.550
What do you have?

00:15:06.850 --> 00:15:08.550
You'll see.

00:15:09.150 --> 00:15:11.800
Say, mind if I invite Tazuki, too?

00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:14.140
I want to show him the dragon.

00:15:14.140 --> 00:15:16.430
He's always wanted to see one.

00:15:16.430 --> 00:15:18.560
I bet he'd be really happy.

00:15:21.070 --> 00:15:23.840
Are you two close outside of school, too?

00:15:23.840 --> 00:15:24.760
Yeah.

00:15:24.760 --> 00:15:27.640
We've been friends ever since preschool.

00:15:27.640 --> 00:15:29.070
Wow...

00:15:29.070 --> 00:15:33.870
When I was little, I was mostly 
at home when my dad was out.

00:15:34.190 --> 00:15:38.560
I always wound up alone when 
the preschool was closed.

00:15:38.560 --> 00:15:40.800
Tazuki seemed to be able to tell.

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:43.400
Kashiwagi-kun.

00:15:45.740 --> 00:15:47.920
We're meeting at my place tomorrow.

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:49.620
You'd better come, or I'll get mad.

00:15:50.910 --> 00:15:52.340
Promise me?

00:15:53.860 --> 00:15:54.590
Okay.

00:15:55.020 --> 00:15:56.660
And in elementary school,

00:16:00.270 --> 00:16:02.350
and even when we entered middle school,

00:16:03.360 --> 00:16:05.790
he always stuck around with me.

00:16:06.660 --> 00:16:10.280
Even since I moved to my current 
place, he comes to hang out a lot.

00:16:12.350 --> 00:16:15.320
He looks cold because he's so collected,

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:19.240
but he's actually always been really kind.

00:16:21.690 --> 00:16:23.250
That's beautiful.

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:24.170
Yeah.

00:16:24.170 --> 00:16:25.780
I'm really grateful.

00:16:34.500 --> 00:16:35.510
I'm home.

00:16:42.330 --> 00:16:45.770
Is that the stuffed toy you 
always bring to school?

00:16:47.940 --> 00:16:49.530
"She saw me."

00:16:49.530 --> 00:16:51.120
It can move?

00:16:55.950 --> 00:16:57.870
Who's that?

00:16:58.280 --> 00:16:58.990
Pretend to be a stuffed toy

00:16:59.030 --> 00:17:00.040
Our promise

00:16:59.780 --> 00:17:00.540
So happy he's home

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:01.580
Staying at home alone

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:02.250
Can't cry

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:03.040
Story book

00:17:02.450 --> 00:17:03.790
Good job on the lizard's bandage

00:17:03.160 --> 00:17:03.790
Pretend to be a stuffed toy

00:17:03.330 --> 00:17:03.790
Our promise

00:17:03.540 --> 00:17:03.790
So happy...

00:17:07.640 --> 00:17:08.540
Mii-kun?!

00:17:08.950 --> 00:17:11.150
Sorry, I scared you, huh?

00:17:11.150 --> 00:17:12.600
Don't cry.

00:17:12.600 --> 00:17:14.770
Good boy, you stayed home alone.

00:17:20.980 --> 00:17:24.550
I can't believe mummies and 
dragons actually exist.

00:17:25.440 --> 00:17:27.750
I'm glad you believe me.

00:17:28.110 --> 00:17:32.190
Yeah, it's like I'm in a 
picture book. It's exciting.

00:17:32.420 --> 00:17:35.350
There are all kinds of species 
living all over the place.

00:17:35.350 --> 00:17:38.950
People don't know about them, 
but they're just like animals.

00:17:38.950 --> 00:17:41.580
But try not to tell people about it.

00:17:42.090 --> 00:17:44.730
They mostly live in secret from humans.

00:17:45.450 --> 00:17:47.240
Why are they hiding?

00:17:48.440 --> 00:17:50.460
This isn't a pleasant thing to say,

00:17:51.330 --> 00:17:54.990
but if people found out that 
imaginary creatures actually exist,

00:17:54.990 --> 00:17:57.720
the world could end up in a panic.

00:17:58.060 --> 00:18:01.190
There might be people who try to capture them

00:18:01.190 --> 00:18:04.650
or use them for profit.

00:18:04.650 --> 00:18:06.090
I see.

00:18:09.570 --> 00:18:10.480
It's Tazuki.

00:18:14.650 --> 00:18:17.620
You look awfully happy. 
What are you plotting?

00:18:17.620 --> 00:18:18.360
Huh?

00:18:18.360 --> 00:18:19.380
A blindfold.

00:18:19.380 --> 00:18:20.330
For who?

00:18:20.330 --> 00:18:21.350
For you.

00:18:21.810 --> 00:18:22.660
What?

00:18:23.280 --> 00:18:25.820
I'm not blindfolding you?

00:18:25.820 --> 00:18:29.620
I'm <i>pretty</i> sure I'm better 
at tying it than you are.

00:18:29.620 --> 00:18:30.870
I'm sure.

00:18:30.870 --> 00:18:33.300
I don't have any intention 
of competing on that.

00:18:33.800 --> 00:18:36.640
I'll take you to what I want to show you.

00:18:37.900 --> 00:18:39.680
Oh, he came out.

00:18:41.090 --> 00:18:43.100
He was in my room.

00:18:43.100 --> 00:18:46.850
You've always said you wanted 
to see a dragon, remember?

00:18:46.850 --> 00:18:47.900
So...

00:18:55.760 --> 00:18:57.030
What's wrong?

00:18:57.480 --> 00:19:00.020
No, it's nothing.

00:19:01.500 --> 00:19:03.650
You had one, too, huh, Tacchan?

00:19:04.050 --> 00:19:05.130
Conny.

00:19:06.570 --> 00:19:09.140
Oni children are omnivorous. 
They'll eat anything.

00:19:09.140 --> 00:19:12.010
But dragon individuals have different diets.

00:19:12.610 --> 00:19:13.820
Huh...

00:19:18.010 --> 00:19:19.820
Looks like he doesn't like meat.

00:19:20.390 --> 00:19:21.680
How about vegetables, then?

00:19:21.990 --> 00:19:23.330
Asparagus?

00:19:23.980 --> 00:19:24.970
Celery?

00:19:25.760 --> 00:19:26.430
Eggplant?

00:19:26.560 --> 00:19:27.430
Rice?

00:19:27.560 --> 00:19:28.430
Oranges?

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:29.440
Cheese?

00:19:29.440 --> 00:19:30.860
No good.

00:19:31.340 --> 00:19:33.090
He won't eat anything.

00:19:34.190 --> 00:19:36.860
Don't give him dog food, Mii-kun.

00:19:37.990 --> 00:19:40.200
You don't have to force yourself!

00:19:41.460 --> 00:19:43.460
I wonder what else we could try.

00:19:44.070 --> 00:19:45.560
How about this?

00:19:45.560 --> 00:19:47.370
Here, say "ahh."

00:19:47.680 --> 00:19:49.500
Good morning, Sora-kun—

00:19:51.520 --> 00:19:53.270
Kaede-san, this is...

00:19:53.270 --> 00:19:55.840
Sora-kun brought a girl over!

00:19:55.840 --> 00:19:56.830
<i>That's</i> what shocked you?

00:19:57.690 --> 00:19:58.990
I'm Motegi Asa.

00:19:58.990 --> 00:20:00.260
Thank you for having me.

00:20:00.930 --> 00:20:03.070
Oh, she's my aunt.

00:20:03.070 --> 00:20:04.660
Kashiwagi Kaede.

00:20:04.660 --> 00:20:07.060
Thank you for taking care of Sora-kun.

00:20:11.310 --> 00:20:13.970
<i>She's so pretty.</i>

00:20:14.460 --> 00:20:16.640
<i>She's so cute.</i>

00:20:17.030 --> 00:20:18.910
Your face is melting.

00:20:20.470 --> 00:20:21.690
I see.

00:20:21.690 --> 00:20:24.320
So you were trying to find 
out what the dragon eats.

00:20:24.740 --> 00:20:28.390
So far, he seems to be 
okay with natto and tofu.

00:20:28.390 --> 00:20:30.100
That seems pretty healthy.

00:20:31.710 --> 00:20:34.040
Looks like Mii-kun managed 
to eat the acai berry.

00:20:34.040 --> 00:20:36.060
His bandage is a mess!

00:20:36.060 --> 00:20:37.590
Oh, it's fine.

00:20:37.990 --> 00:20:42.000
I recently found out that no matter 
how dirty it gets, it comes right off.

00:20:42.850 --> 00:20:44.970
<i>So that's where his mouth is.</i>

00:20:46.030 --> 00:20:49.800
So what are you going to name the dragon?

00:20:49.800 --> 00:20:51.770
I already have one for him.

00:20:51.770 --> 00:20:54.930
There's a name I've always 
wanted to give a pet.

00:20:54.930 --> 00:20:56.880
Huh, what's the name?

00:20:58.160 --> 00:20:59.140
Isao.

00:21:01.520 --> 00:21:04.430
Okay, I'm going to walk 
Motegi-san and Isao home.

00:21:04.430 --> 00:21:05.570
Thank you for having me.

00:21:05.570 --> 00:21:07.740
Come visit again.

00:21:09.170 --> 00:21:11.750
Why did Mii-kun come to 
your place, Sora-chan?

00:21:11.960 --> 00:21:14.270
My dad sent him.

00:21:14.270 --> 00:21:16.990
My dad's a self-proclaimed adventurer.

00:21:16.990 --> 00:21:19.050
He knows a lot about 
these kinds of creatures.

00:21:19.940 --> 00:21:22.010
It's not that Mii-kun came on his own.

00:21:25.070 --> 00:21:29.980
<i>If that's the case, why doesn't 
Mii-kun want to go back to Egypt?</i>

00:21:31.200 --> 00:21:33.270
He's so prone to loneliness.

00:21:33.700 --> 00:21:36.200
Could he really be okay

00:21:36.200 --> 00:21:39.020
being torn away from his birthplace?

00:21:39.900 --> 00:21:44.530
Come to think of it, when I tried to 
send him back home, he got really upset.

00:21:45.610 --> 00:21:46.960
What's wrong?

00:21:49.420 --> 00:21:50.530
It's nothing.

00:21:51.500 --> 00:21:54.220
I wonder why Isao came to my place.

00:21:54.740 --> 00:21:56.580
I'm not sure.

00:21:57.640 --> 00:22:02.120
But Isao must be relieved to have 
met you, though, Motegi-san.

00:22:03.040 --> 00:22:04.830
I mean, look.

00:22:13.080 --> 00:22:13.870
Yeah.

00:23:50.350 --> 00:23:54.230
We all watched a horror movie together, 
and Mii-kun became catatonic.

00:23:54.230 --> 00:23:57.030
I guess even mummies get scared 
watching horror movies.

00:23:57.030 --> 00:24:00.250
Mii-kun's soul was half 
way out of his mouth.

00:23:59.660 --> 00:24:04.670
Next Episode
I can't grow all at once, 
so I'll grow over time

00:24:00.810 --> 00:24:02.000
<i>How to Keep a Mummy</i>.

00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:03.450
See you next time.

00:24:04.670 --> 00:24:07.660
<b>See you next time!</b>
